The data travels **separately**: the DBMS compiles the SQL statement first, then binds the values:

~~~js
// Node + better-sqlite3 / pg
db.prepare("SELECT name FROM customers WHERE phone = ?").get(input);
await pool.query("SELECT name FROM customers WHERE phone = $1", [input]);
~~~

`' OR '1'='1` is now just an unfamiliar phone-number string. It matches no one.
